# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT — WINDOWS 11 MULTI-MORPHISM DESIGN SYSTEM WITH SYSTEM ADMINISTRATOR WORKSPACE

## 1. Project Objective

Completely transform the existing application's UI/UX into a premium, Windows 11-inspired application featuring a role-aware, multi-morphism design architecture.

Implement eight design styles — Skeuomorphism, Flat Design, Neumorphism, Material Design, Glassmorphism, Claymorphism, Neubrutalism, and Polymorphism — and intelligently assign them to actual user roles, workspaces, and interactions.

**System Administrator must be explicitly included as a first-class role in the design architecture.** It must receive a dedicated, powerful, security-oriented administrative workspace with its own visual identity, global system controls, and appropriate access to existing administrative capabilities.

The entire application must feel like a carefully engineered desktop operating environment rather than a generic website.

Preserve the existing business logic, routes, data, integrations, authentication, permissions, and application features. Redesign the entire interface, not just the landing page.

