## 7. Role Detection and Authorization

Build role-aware styling on top of the existing trusted authentication and authorization system.

- Load the authenticated user's permitted roles and current active role.
- Resolve the appropriate design configuration centrally.
- Apply role-specific design tokens to shared components.
- Update the visual system when a supported role switch occurs.
- Keep protected routes and administrative actions enforced by the existing authorization architecture.
- Ensure client-side theme selection never grants access to privileged capabilities.
- Avoid exposing administrative commands or sensitive data to unauthorized users.
- Do not create new authentication mechanisms or duplicate the existing role model unnecessarily.

The visual identity communicates the active workspace; it must never substitute for actual authorization.

